{"slug":"Personal Monopoly","title":"Personal Monopoly.md","sourceUrl":"https://mathnuscript.com/fleeting-notes/personal-monopoly","publishedAt":"2023-12-08T18:14:19.428Z","words":38,"readingTime":1,"html":"<p>There is a concept by <a href=\"https://mathnuscript.com/david-perell\" class=\"internal internal-link alias\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">David Perell</a> in this <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=08S67KEb6hQ\" class=\"external external-link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">video<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"external-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\"><path d=\"M320 0H288V64h32 82.7L201.4 265.4 178.7 288 224 333.3l22.6-22.6L448 109.3V192v32h64V192 32 0H480 320zM32 32H0V64 480v32H32 456h32V480 352 320H424v32 96H64V96h96 32V32H160 32z\"></path></svg></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://mathnuscript.com/ikigai\" class=\"internal internal-link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ikigai</a> is also similar in nature but not quite.</p>\n<p>My personal monoploy can consist of the following in 2022 to 2023:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><a href=\"https://mathnuscript.com/computation\" class=\"internal internal-link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Computation</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mathnuscript.com/knowledge\" class=\"internal internal-link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Knowledge</a> and <a href=\"https://mathnuscript.com/philosophy\" class=\"internal internal-link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Philosophy</a> (<a href=\"https://mathnuscript.com/epistemology\" class=\"internal internal-link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Epistemology</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mathnuscript.com/product-development\" class=\"internal internal-link alias\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Product Development</a></li>\n</ol>","toc":[]}